From 91e5d3570a69ef96c1b714f664945cf8313a51b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: milliluk-erik <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:41:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] breakpoint: physical instruction breakpoints, and a gdb

The stop reply here first said 'T' only on a GIME machine and fell back
to a bare S%02x everywhere else.  That shape made the GIME branch the
only place to hang additional stop-reply fields, so every later
machine-independent field would silently vanish for the Dragon family.
Restructured: every machine sends a T packet (with no pairs when there
is no MMU -- valid RSP, and clients accept it), the MMU pairs are added
only when a GIME exists, and the physical PC is computed for every
machine, degrading to the logical PC on a flat machine exactly as
trap_fast_phys() does fork-wide.
